---
title: Lab 4.1 - Basic Async/Await Flow
---

flowchart TD
    A[Main Thread] --> B[Call Async Method]

    B --> C[async Method]
    C --> D[await Operation]
    D --> E[Return Control to Caller]

    E --> F[Operation Completes]
    F --> G[Resume Method Execution]

    G --> H[Method Returns Task]

    subgraph "Async Method Lifecycle"
        I[Method Called] --> J[Execute Until await]
        J --> K[Capture Context]
        K --> L[Start Async Operation]
        L --> M[Return Incomplete Task]
        M --> N[Operation Completes]
        N --> O[Schedule Continuation]
        O --> P[Resume on Captured Context]
    end

    subgraph "Task Coordination"
        Q[Task.WhenAll] --> R[Start All Tasks]
        R --> S[Wait for All Complete]
        S --> T[Return Results Array]

        U[Task.WhenAny] --> V[Start All Tasks]
        V --> W[Wait for First Complete]
        W --> X[Return First Task]
    end

    subgraph "Async Patterns"
        Y[async Task Method] --> Z[Return Task]
        AA[async Task&lt;T&gt; Method] --> BB[Return Task&lt;T&gt;]
        CC[async void Method] --> DD[Fire-and-Forget]
    end

    subgraph "I/O Operations"
        EE[File.ReadAllTextAsync] --> FF[Non-blocking File I/O]
        GG[HttpClient.GetAsync] --> HH[Non-blocking Network I/O]
        II[Task.Delay] --> JJ[Non-blocking Delay]
    end